  ## What it provides

  - Remote access to the approved Building OS MCP tool catalogue.
  - No LAN browsing, subnet access, arbitrary device access, shell access, or VPN.
  - WireGuard remains a separate site-to-site and technician-access system.
  - Public access keys terminate at the vendor server. They are never forwarded to the client.
  - The vendor request is converted into a bounded protocol frame and carried through the existing outbound
    client session.

  - The client injects its separate internal MCP key before forwarding to port 7087.
  - Tool handlers then call the normal site gateway on port 7085.

