  ## Enrollment

  1. The vendor administrator creates a one-time enrollment token for the router serial.
  2. The client reads the live MikroTik serial.
  3. The client generates its connector private key locally.
  4. The client sends the token, serial and connector public credential to vendor /enroll.
  5. The vendor deterministically derives a five-digit site_id from the serial, retrying if the ID is already
     occupied.

  6. That ID becomes both:
      - The public hostname label: <site_id>.ai.lighting
      - The vendor and client loopback routing port.

  7. The vendor stores credential hashes only.
  8. The client stores its credential using Windows DPAPI under the current user.
  9. The serial is checked again every connector start.

  Credential roles are deliberately separate:

   Credential          Purpose
  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
   Vendor admin key    Loopback vendor administration
  ──────────────────  ────────────────────────────────────────────
   Enrollment token    One-time client enrollment
  ──────────────────  ────────────────────────────────────────────
   Connector key       Client-to-vendor WSS session
  ──────────────────  ────────────────────────────────────────────
   Site access key     ChatGPT, Claude or other public MCP caller
  ──────────────────  ────────────────────────────────────────────
   Local MCP key       Client connector to local port 7087

  Default validity is 365 days for enrollment tokens, 365 days for connector credentials and 90 days for public
  site keys. See /C:/Users/danie/building-os/tools/bos-vendor-addon/src/vendor/credentials/types.ts:1 and /C:/
  Users/danie/building-os/host/runtime/server/src/vendor-relay/credential-store.ts:268.

