  Cloudflare is only on the vendor public MCP side. It is not between the client connector and the vendor
  control endpoint.

  Each active site requires an exact Cloudflare origin route such as:

  44354.ai.lighting -> http://127.0.0.1:44354

  Wildcard DNS alone cannot select a different origin port for each site. The code only generates route rows
  and configuration snippets. It does not configure or manage cloudflared.

  ## Runtime safeguards

  - One active connector session per site.
  - Eight in-flight calls per site.
  - Sixteen in-flight calls across one vendor process by default.
  - 1 MiB request limit.
  - 8 MiB response limit.
  - 30-second heartbeat and 90-second stale-session close.
  - Requests are not replayed after uncertain dispatch.
  - Disconnects cancel outstanding work.
  - Authentication and protocol failures are terminal.
  - Site access keys are site-bound and currently have only the mcp scope.
  - Revoking a connector drops its live session.
  - Revoking a site closes its listener, session and associated credentials.

  The broker and request state are memory-only. A vendor restart loses sessions and in-flight calls.

